            "notes": "The power you choose here depends on the team comps.  [Amplification Barrier](item_a04d01ac-ead8-4b78-ba9a-32cc430041a1) can be taken and possibly even swap over to a shield build if you team is coordinated. But like round 2 you want to still choose AD items almost every time. In a team with little to no projectiles  [Barrier Reconstruction](item_ecd5cf3c-0293-42e9-b015-0b00c25082f5) can be taken for extra survivability. Make sure you get  [Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054).  [Heartbeat Sensor](item_2a4ffaf4-f14b-47d2-a267-0a0e83e87418) is ideal but I will take both  [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) and  [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) if this if the money works out. Try to have at least 5 slots filled because the common items give more value for their cost. without  [Wilhelmwagen](item_c6b943ef-1941-4979-81dd-8848a171326e) you might need to get max movement speed. if you have enough get  [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) for the 10% movement speed. At this point you need to focus on objective rather than generating money as this build is not money hungry. you want to win at least 2 of the 3 rounds as round 6 will be tough to win. Round 7 should be relatively easy as long as your team has 2 brain cells.",
