        {
            "id": "5fc374d4-808d-448e-95f9-faf620623e43",
            "build_id": "19793a58-ca9b-4cab-ac05-c031c31ce6f2",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-02T23:29:39.919218+00:00",
            "notes": "I like to go   [Rustung Von Wilhelm](item_aea17a63-3f55-4f91-8f49-a7793fbc56c4)  along with  [Heartbeat Sensor](item_2a4ffaf4-f14b-47d2-a267-0a0e83e87418) .   [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8)  can work instead if the enemy team is not very deadly. for the last slot buy the best item you can afford:  [First Aid Kit](item_0172eaaa-1902-44a3-b989-d12f0f7301da) , [Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054) , or  [Meka Z-Series](item_358d93ab-617b-41e7-8df3-ac78d0d8c680) . I don't think  [Ironclad Cleats](item_afb5c28e-3980-4a7d-85be-785c32217c28) is necessary but Lucio can boop you if they build correctly.\n\nThe play style for this is to stand in front of the enemy tank as much as possible while still protecting your team from flankers and Juno torpedoes. \n\nYour main kill potential is your Earthshatter. Use it as frequently as needed, and a solo shatter is often enough to win unless the enemy has a mercy. (still good idea to solo shatter if it feels hard to get more than 1 person)\n\nSave your charge to stun enemies and kill dps/support that get overzealous. You also need to use charge to peel your backline and for movement. NEVER go for the 1v5 charge into the enemy team unless it is to touch point in overtime.\n\nimportant matchups: \n\n-Juno: always try to block as many torpedoes as you can as this will stop her from recharging her next use of homing torpedoes.\n\n-Genji: this can be one of the hardest matchups as a melee genji can just 1v5 your backline. tell your team to buy  [Iron Eyes](item_f16d03a7-f20e-4a1d-a1f6-55863e163c03) for a cheap way to stop his damage as he will likely have a critical strike on his melee.\n\n-D.Va: this is the worst tank match up currently. D.Va has the mobility to go around your barrier as well as the ability to defense matrix your teams amplified damage. Try to stay close to your team and deny the D.Va from doing damage. The upside to D.Va is that she does not have the best shield break compared to the other tanks.\n\nNote: I have not tested enough against sigma to determine if he is a harder match up than D.Va.",
